    "created_at": "2023-02-17T09:44:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-02-17T10:44:36Z",
    "body": "> Are there any performance results to add to the PR?\r\n\r\nWhen using 16 heads, I expect the kernel to be roughly 16 times faster. Instead of doing 16xGEMM{M=1, N, K} we do 1xGEMM{M=16, N, K}. In practice, we saw ~10-15% more throughput for LLM decoding jobs end-to-end.",
